        "(noirstyle), Generate a film noir scene: 'Brutal Justice, 1950s London'. Color palette: Charcoal Gray (#364F4F) dominant, Gunmetal (#708090) secondary, and Blood Red (#B22222) accents. Capture the gritty realism of a late afternoon in 1950s London. A 35-year-old man, bruised and battered, is subjected to a brutal beating by two menacing prison guards within the dimly lit confines of a British jail cell. Employ harsh contrasts of light and shadow to create a dramatic, suspenseful atmosphere. Use deep blacks and grays to highlight the grimness of the scene, with accents of blood red emphasizing the violence. Focus on the man's stoic expression and the guards' cold, calculated brutality. Render in a gritty, textured style reminiscent of classic film noir photography."
